/* /////////////////////////////////////////////////////

The unlisted per-course Canvas credentials page (/courses/<slug>/canvas),
where an instructor issues their own LTI 1.1 consumer key and secret.

The page renders in the `main` layout, so its styles belong in modules/, which
main.styl picks up by glob. It first shipped borrowing .lti-status-list and
.lti-setup__error from _lti_iframe.styl — a partial kept outside modules/
precisely so that glob cannot sweep it in, since those selectors are only ever
used by the lti_iframe layout. The borrowed rules therefore never reached this
page, and its definition lists rendered as unstyled stacked text.

///////////////////////////////////////////////////// */

// A grid rather than stacked flex rows, so the label column is sized to the
// widest label in whichever list is on screen. The two lists have very
// different labels ("Shared secret" against "Last opened from Canvas"), and a
// fixed label width either ragged-edges one or over-indents the other.
.canvas-credentials__list
  margin 0 0 18px
  display grid
  grid-template-columns max-content 1fr
  gap 10px 16px
  align-items center

  dt
    font-weight 600
    color $text_med

  dd
    margin 0
    min-width 0
    display flex
    flex-wrap wrap
    align-items center
    gap 8px

// A consumer key, a shared secret and a configuration URL all have to be
// copied exactly, and the secret is shown on one render only. So a long value
// wraps instead of clipping: a value the instructor cannot read in full is the
// one thing this page must not produce. The monospace face and the tinted chip
// come from the `code` rule in _base.styl.
.canvas-credentials__value
  word-break break-all
  padding .4em .5em

.canvas-credentials__copy
  flex-shrink 0

// Shown on the single render that carries the shared secret, where the
// instructor has one chance to copy it.
.canvas-credentials__warning
  margin 0 0 18px
  padding 12px 16px
  border-radius 6px
  background $warning-background
  border 1px solid $warning_border
  color $warning_text

  p
    margin 0
